<p align="center"><font face="helvetica, arial" size="4" color="00ff00"><b>Guild Rules</b></font>
</td>
<td>
<font face="helvetica, arial" size="2"><b>
<ol type="1">
	<li>All good and evil worshipers are allowed in Soldiers of Destiny. It is not anyone’s place within SoD to tell someone what to or what not to kill.<br><br>
	<li>A new member to Soldiers of Destiny must be of the 20th season/circle, with the following exceptions:
		<ol type="A">
			<li>Person(s) has/have a character within the guild already.
			<li>Person(s) has/have a character of the 20th season/circle or higher outside the guild.
			<li>Person(s) is/are close real life friends whom you accept total responsibility for (i.e. help them learn the game, answer questions for them, teach them how to research things about EverQuest, etc.)
**All new members must have a sponsor within Soldiers of Destiny for the time of their trial period (2 weeks). Sponsors are responsible for this/these person(s) for that time period. They are to ensure the new member receives important information (i.e. how to register on the guild website and maintain their information) in a timely fashion.
		</ol><br><br>
	<li>Absolutely NO KILL STEALING, NINJA LOOTING, BEGGING OR SPAMMING OF CHAT CHANNELS! Any members caught doing this will be put on probation. Take personal problems to /tell or use /ignore <username>. Racism (using real life terms to degrade someone’s ethic background/heritage) is NOT tolerated and will result in termination of your guild status… However roleplaying is definitely allowed.<br><br>
	<li>Loot amongst guildmates: Items dropped off of mobs shall be rolled on a "need before greed" (NBG) basis. If you already have something better, do not roll on it, let another member of the group/guild have a chance at upgrading their gear. If no one in the group can use the item and it is not NO DROP, all shall have a chance to roll on it, provided they have not already won something, unless otherwise discussed and agreed upon by the party members.<br><br>
	<li>Hierarchy currently consists of:<br><br>
		<i>Guild Leader:</i> Bobmd Cureall<br><br>
		<i>Assistant Guild Leader:</i> Kluuvan<br><br>
		<i>Guild Mother: Alailya</i><br><br>
 		<i>Officers:</i> Nighon, Halguran, Cedari, Delylah<br><br>
		<i>Cadets: Jove, Coldrain, Beelorn, Xetus</i><br><br>
     	<i>Guild Elders:</i><br>
		Palelf Wrathhammer (Retired: Officer)<br>
		Nandarin Stormheart (Retired: Guild Leader)<br>
		Vinstad Valenwood (Retired: Asst. Guild Leader)<br>
		Brogzog Thumpton (Retired: Officer)<br>
		Crankmor Damedge (Retired: Officer) Aka Shaitana Vee<br><br>
		
<i>Note: Guild Elders are responsible for voting on issues that are tied between the Leaders and Officers of Soldiers of Destiny.</i><br><br>
	<li>If any rules are broken you may be put on probation or removed from the guild depending on the severity of the action. Appropriate action will be discussed amongst the Elders and the Officers of Soldiers of Destiny.<br><br>
	<li>You may leave Soldiers of Destiny at any time. An explanation of why you are leaving is appreciated greatly, but none is necessary. Influencing others to leave will result in a recommendation not so honorable. Others should leave guilds on their own terms. Not someone else’s. Re-entering the guild will be voted on by the Elders and the Officers of Soldiers of Destiny.
</ol>
<p align="center">
